Z||000000||Countach||09-21-2001||12:44 AM||||I bought an '85 GT out of a junk yard that had been hit in the right front tire.  I've replaced the knuckle joint, ball joint, inner fender panel, hood and fender and got it driveable again.<BR>  The way the panels fit makes me think it's got some frame damage.  Is this worth repairing?  It runs good and has a PERFECT interior (new seats, Corsa steering wheel).<BR>Thanks, John||||reg||7
Z||000001||Cheever3000||09-21-2001||12:49 AM||||My 88GT needed some right front straightening after I tried to go into the Astrodome without knocking.  Cost me $250 and wasn't perfect (he told me it wouldn't be) but it did the trick and was worth every penny.  I should have pulled that part of the wiring harness first, cause they melted some of it, but so far everything works.<BR>||||reg||1
